# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets. Never commit these.
#
# An agent holds a Gemini key, a Tavily key and an HF token. A leaked key in
# git history survives `git rm` and has to be rotated, so this block is first
# and gitleaks runs in pre-commit and CI as a second line of defence.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
secrets.json
.secrets/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Agent runtime artifacts.
#
# Session workspaces hold whatever the file tool wrote and whatever the sandbox
# spilled -- untrusted content by definition. Trajectories embed full tool
# arguments and results, which is exactly where a key would end up if the
# redaction in trajectory/redact.py ever regressed. Neither belongs in history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
sessions/
workspaces/
trajectories/
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db

# Pyodide downloads its wheels on first run; reproducible, ~200MB, not ours.
.pyodide_cache/
node_modules/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data: committed selectively.
#
# The eval task set, the gold annotations and the attack corpus ARE committed
# on purpose -- they are the evidence behind every number in the README, and a
# result you cannot re-derive is not a result. Recorded replays and the LLM
# response cache are large, machine-generated, and regenerable, so they stay
# out. Anything not explicitly un-ignored below is ignored by default.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/*
!data/eval/
!data/attacks/
!data/fixtures/
data/fixtures/llm_cache.sqlite
data/replays/
data/scratch/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Evaluation
#
# eval results ARE committed -- the run history is the evidence behind the
# results table. Only scratch output and the resume ledger are ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
eval_results/scratch/
.eval_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/
.installed.cfg

# Environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Tooling caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.hypothesis/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Gradio
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.gradio/
flagged/

# Sweep console output. Operational noise -- the durable record of a run is
# trajectories/runs.jsonl and eval_results/, both of which are structured.
*.log
